,"H5800":"forsake","H6177":"Aroer","H5739":"flock","H7257":"to stretch","H369":"nothing","H2729":"to tremble","H7673":"to cease","H4013":"fortification","H669":"Ephraim","H4467":"kingdom","H7605":"remnant","H758":"Aram","H3519":"glory","H1121":"child","H3478":"Israel","H5002":"utterance","H3068":"LORD","H6635":"army","H3117":"day","H1931":"he/she/it","H1809":"to languish","H3290":"Jacob","H4924":"fat","H1320":"flesh","H7329":"to starve","H622":"to gather","H7105":"harvest","H7054":"standing grain","H2220":"arm","H7641":"stream","H7114":"be short","H3950":"to gather","H6010":"Valley (of Achor)","H7497":"Rapha","H7604":"to remain","H5955":"gleaning","H5363":"shaking","H2132":"(Mount of) Olives","H8147":"two","H7969":"three","H1620":"berry","H7218":"head","H534":"top","H702":"four","H2568":"five","H5585":"cleft","H6509":"be fruitful","H430":"God","H8159":"to gaze","H120":"man","H5921":"upon","H6213":"do","H5869":"eye","H413":"to(wards)","H6918":"holy","H7200":"see","H3808":"not","H4196":"altar","H4639":"work","H3027":"hand","H834":"which","H676":"finger","H842":"Asherah","H2553":"pillar","H4581":"security","H2793":"Horesh","H6440":"before","H8077":"devastation","H3588":"for","H7911":"to forget","H3468":"salvation","H6697":"Rocks (of Goats)","H2142":"to remember","H3651":"right","H5193":"to plant","H5194":"plantation","H5282":"pleasantness","H2156":"branch","H2114":"be a stranger","H2232":"to sow","H7735":"to grow","H1242":"morning","H2233":"seed","H6524":"to sprout","H5067":"heap","H2470":"weak","H3511":"pain","H605":"be incurable","H1945":"woe!","H1995":"crowd","H5971":"people","H7227":"many","H1993":"to roar","H3220":"sea","H7588":"roar","H3816":"people","H4325":"water","H3524":"mighty","H7582":"to crash","H1605":"to rebuke","H5127":"to flee","H4801":"distance","H7291":"to pursue","H4671":"chaff","H2022":"mount","H7307":"spirit","H1534":"wheel","H5492":"whirlwind","H6256":"time","H6153":"evening","H1091":"terror","H2962":"before","H2088":"this","H2506":"portion","H8154":"to plunder","H1486":"allotted","H962":"to plunder"},"ccc":{},"cccp":{},"com":[["haydock",1,null,"haydock","Damascus. When it was taken by Theglathphalassar, or rather by Sennacherib, chap. x. 8. It was again ruined by Nabuchodonosor, Jeremias xlix. 24. But after the first taking, it never regained its power. Magni nominis umbra. (Calmet)"],["haydock",2,null,"haydock","Aroer. Chaldean, “abandoned, shall be folds for sheep.” Septuagint, “left for ever a resting place for flocks and herds, and none shall pursue.” The tribes on the east of the Jordan shall be led captive, as well as those on the west, Ephraim, &c. (Haydock)"],["haydock",3,null,"haydock","Damascus. Their too great union proved their ruin. Sennacherib took Damascus, as Salmanasar had done Samaria."],["haydock",4,null,"haydock","Lean. All the power of the kingdom shall fail, as in a mortal illness."],["haydock",5,null,"haydock","Raphaim. Near Jerusalem, 3 Kings xxiii. 13. Septuagint, “of stones.” (Calmet) — It will be equally difficult to find any men left in the kingdom of Israel. (Haydock)"],["haydock",7,null,"haydock","Israel. They obeyed the summons of Ezechias and of Josias, (2 Paralipomenon xxx. 1., and xxxiv. 6.) and every after followed the same worship as Juda. (Calmet)"],["haydock",9,null,"haydock","Left. By the Chanaanites, when the children of Israel came into their land. (Challoner) — Their consternation was become proverbial, Josue ii. 9., and v. 11."],["haydock",10,null,"haydock","Good. Septuagint, “fruitless.” Israel had abandoned the Lord; and could expect nothing but the fruits of death. (Calmet)"],["haydock",11,null,"haydock","Much. Thou hast laboured earnestly, but reaped no benefit. (Haydock)"],["haydock",12,null,"haydock","Multitude, &c. This and all that follows to the end of the chapter, relates to the Assyrian army under Sennacherib, (Challoner) or rather to that of Israel and its allies. (Calmet) — After the Assyrians had afflicted Israel, they were also punished. (Worthington)"],["haydock",14,null,"haydock","Not be. Phacee and Rasin were presently exterminated. — Spoiled us. The kingdom of Achaz, 4 Kings xvii. 5."],["challoner",9,null,"challoner","That were left.... Viz., by the Chanaanites, when the children of Israel came into their land."],["challoner",12,null,"challoner","The multitude, etc.... This and all that follows to the end of the chapter, relates to the Assyrian army under Sennacherib."]],"au":{"haydock":["George Leo Haydock",0,0,1849,"https://www.newadvent.org/cathen/07160a.htm"],"challoner":["Richard Challoner",0,0,1781,"https://www.newadvent.org/cathen/03566a.htm"]},"fa":[[4,8,0,"The Proof of the Gospel","Book 2",0,339,"… 5. And it shall be as when one gathers standing corn, and reaps the grain of the ears; 6. And it shall be as when one gathers ears in a rich valley, and stubble is left. Or as the berries of an olive tree are left, two or three on the topmost bough, or four or five on its branches, thus saith the Lord God of Israel. 7. In that day a man shall trust in him that made him, and his eyes shall look on the Holy One of Israel, 8. and they shall not trust in the altars, nor in the work of their hands, which their own fingers have made.\" …"]],"fau":[["eusebius","Eusebius of Caesarea",0,"ecclesiastical-writer",null,1,339]],"ftr":[["W. J. Ferrar, The Proof of the Gospel (SPCK, 1920)"]]}